# Player Gameplay UI

The Player Gameplay UI provides the player with real-time feedback on their status, resources, and available actions.

The UI is designed to be minimal, readable, and always visible, ensuring the player can make informed decisions without interrupting gameplay.

---

##  Core UI Layout

The UI is divided into key areas of the screen:

- Top Left — Financial & Rent Information  
- Top Right — Time & Day Tracking  
- Bottom Left — Player Stats  
- Bottom Center — Inventory Slots  

---

##  Financial & Objective UI (Top Left)

Displays:

- Rent Due  
- Days Remaining for Rent  
- Current Money  

### Purpose:
- Keeps financial pressure visible at all times  
- Reinforces urgency and long-term goals  

---

##  Time System UI (Top Right)

Displays:

- Current Time  
- Day of the Week  
- Current Day Count  

### Purpose:
- Helps the player plan daily activities  
- Reinforces time as a limited resource  

---

##  Player Stats UI (Bottom Left)

Tracks core player attributes:

- Stress
- Morale
- Stamina

### Behavior:
- Updates in real time based on player actions  
- Uses color-coded bars for quick readability  

### Purpose:
- Provides immediate feedback on player condition  
- Influences available actions and decisions  

---

##  Inventory UI (Bottom Center)

- Displays available inventory slots  
- Items appear when collected (e.g. medicine, food)  
- Items are removed when used  

### Purpose:
- Enables resource management  
- Connects directly to gameplay systems (Grandpa care, survival)

---

###  City Awareness Feed (Planned)

- Displays discovered events in the city  
- Updates based on exploration and player encounters  

### Purpose:
- Reinforces the discovery-based world system  
- Keeps track of growing dissent  

---

###  End-of-Day Summary (Planned)

Displays:

- Money earned  
- Stress changes  
- Grandpa condition  
- City updates  

### Purpose:
- Reinforces consequences of daily decisions  
- Provides player reflection before the next day  

---

##  UI System Integration

The UI directly reflects changes in all major gameplay systems:

- Job System → Money, Stress  
- Grandpa System → Health, Feedback Messages  
- Time System → Clock & Day Progression  
- Inventory System → Item availability  
- City System → Future UI (news/events)  

---

##  Design Goal

The UI is designed to:

- Deliver critical information without overwhelming the player  
- Support fast decision-making  
- Reinforce tension between systems  
- Maintain immersion while providing clarity  

